  "answer": "The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Changes to `ranges.mjs`\n\nI rewrote `mergeRanges(ranges)` to satisfy all requirements:\n\n**Validation (throws `TypeError`):**\n- Input must be an array.\n- Each element must be an array of exactly length 2.\n- Both bounds must be safe integers (`Number.isSafeInteger`).\n- `start <= end` must hold.\n\n**Correct merging:**\n- **No mutation:** Input pairs are copied via `.map(([start, end]) => [start, end])` before sorting, so the original array and its pairs are never touched.\n- **Sort by start, then end:** `sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0] || a[1] - b[1])`.\n- **Overlap or adjacency:** merge when `range[0] <= last[1] + 1`, so `[2,4]` and `[5,7]` become `[2,7]`.\n- **Contained intervals don't shorten:** the end is only extended when `range[1] > last[1]`, so a contained interval like `[3,4]` inside `[1,5]` leaves the result as `[1,5]`.\n- **Fresh output:** the result array and every pair in it are newly created arrays.\n- **Empty input:** returns `[]`.\n- **Named export** `mergeRanges` is preserved.\n\nThe two provided tests (`unsorted overlaps merge in order` and `adjacent integer intervals touch`) pass with this logic.",
